A graphical display of a numeric value within a known range.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/meter)

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Meter(value: 64) do
  MeterLabel { "Storage" }
  MeterValue()
  MeterProgress()
end
```

A Meter displays a static measurement inside a known range (disk usage, a score, remaining battery), as opposed
to [Progress](<%= page_path(:progress) %>), which tracks a task toward completion. `MeterLabel` names the
reading, `MeterValue` prints the formatted number and `MeterProgress` draws the track and fill. The root lays
them out on a grid - label top-left, value top-right, track underneath - so include only the parts you need.

The fill uses the primary accent. Pass `low:`, `high:` and `optimum:` and it recolors itself to signal whether
the reading is good, borderline or bad - green, amber or red.

## Examples

### Status thresholds

The indicator colors by zone: optimum (green) when the value sits in the same zone as `optimum:`, suboptimum
(amber) one zone away, invalid (red) at the far end. `optimum: 10` marks low usage as healthy.

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :status %>

### Formatting the value

`format:` takes `Intl.NumberFormat` options in snake_case - currency, a unit, and so on. The server formats the
first render; live updates use the browser's `Intl.NumberFormat` with the same options. For full control, give
`MeterValue` a block: it receives the formatted string and the raw value.

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :formatting %>

```ruby
Meter(value: 3.4, max: 8, format: { style: :unit, unit: "gigabyte", maximum_fraction_digits: 1 }) do
  MeterValue { |formatted, _value| "#{formatted} of 8 GB" }
end
```

### Password strength (controlled)

Score the input as the user types and set the meter's value; the `ui--meter` controller moves the fill,
recolors it and updates the text and ARIA. `MeterValue(labels:)` prints a word for each value.

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :password_strength %>

```js
meter.setAttribute("data-ui--meter-value-value", score(input.value))
```

### Minimal

Drop `MeterValue` (and even `MeterLabel`) for a bare track, and restyle the parts with `class:`.

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :minimal %>

### RTL

The label and value swap sides and the track fills from the right.

<%= embed UI::MeterPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

When a threshold is set the root exposes `data-status` (`optimum` | `suboptimum` | `invalid`); the fill
carries `data-slot="meter-indicator"` with the status background class.

### Meter

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `value:` | `Numeric` | - | Required. The current value. |
| `min:` | `Numeric` | `0` | Lower bound of the range. |
| `max:` | `Numeric` | `100` | Upper bound of the range. |
| `low:` | `Numeric` | - | Upper edge of the "low" zone. Enables status coloring. |
| `high:` | `Numeric` | - | Lower edge of the "high" zone. Enables status coloring. |
| `optimum:` | `Numeric` | - | The ideal value; its zone becomes the green one. Enables status coloring. |
| `status_classes:` | `{ optimum:, suboptimum:, invalid:, default: }` | - | Override the fill class per status (and the no-threshold default). |
| `format:` | `Hash` (Intl.NumberFormat options) | percent | Formatting of the displayed value: `style: :percent / :currency / :unit / :decimal`, `currency:`, `unit:`, `maximum_fraction_digits:`, `minimum_fraction_digits:`. |
| `locale:` | `String` | browser's | Locale for live updates (`Intl.NumberFormat`). |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | - | Name the meter when there's no `MeterLabel`. |

Other attributes go to the `role="meter"` root; `class:` is merged (override the grid layout here).

### MeterLabel, MeterProgress

A `<span>` wired to the root with `aria-labelledby`, and the track `<div>` holding the fill. `class:` is merged.

### MeterValue

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `labels:` | `Array<String>` | - | Words indexed by the (rounded) value instead of the number - also used for live updates. |
| block | `\|formatted, value\|` | - | Build the text yourself. |

## Accessibility

- Meter renders `role="meter"` with `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax` and a formatted
  `aria-valuetext` ("$1,280.00" rather than a bare number).
- Give every meter a name - a `MeterLabel` (wired via `aria-labelledby`) or `aria_label:` on the root.
- Color alone shouldn't carry meaning - pair the status colors with the value or a word.
- The fill transition honors `prefers-reduced-motion`.
